{"seq":1,"mint":"F21","verb":"fact","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-6-luna","approach":"split","literals":true,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"The label is built in three separate arms of the `match lines` (whole file; out-of-range; in-range), each writing its own format string.","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F21"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"        None => (contents.clone(), path.to_string()),\n        Some((a, b)) => {\n            if a < 1 || a > b {\n                return Err(workspace::refuse(workspace_dir, \"look\", format!(\"invalid --lines range {a}:{b}\")));\n            }\n            let all: Vec<&str> = contents.lines().collect();\n            let total = all.len();\n            if a > total {\n                (String::new(), format!(\"{path} lines {a}-{b} (file has {total} line(s); nothing in range)\"))\n            } else {\n                let end = b.min(total);\n                (all[a - 1..end].join(\"\\n\"), format!(\"{path} lines {a}-{end}\"))\n            }\n        }\n    };","why":"The match has two arms, `None` and `Some`; the out-of-range and in-range cases are branches inside `Some`. The whole-file label uses `path.to_string()`, not a format string.","quoted":true}],"at":1790153877,"cost":0.007741026,"elapsed_ms":110677,"attempts":5,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0,"typed_versions":["jev-1.13.0"],"gate_calls":1}
